    "description": "<h2>Source of truth</h2><p>https://jumpr.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JK/pages/269090817/03+User+Stories+Jira+Disposition</p><h2>Outcome</h2><p>A Deal keeps ownership of its business makeup through every non-terminal lifecycle state. <strong>Archived</strong> releases only the deduplication key; each Deal record keeps its permanent External Deal ID.</p><h2>Rules</h2><h3>Deal Makeup Key</h3><ul><li><p>System-managed and unique.</p></li><li><p>Draft, Active, Paused, Inactive and Closed retain the raw makeup key.</p></li><li><p>Only Archived releases it.</p></li><li><p>Preferred new implementation form if not already deployed: <code>{raw}-A-{18-character CASESAFEID}</code>.</p></li><li><p>Retaining an existing deployed <code>-R-</code> internal suffix is acceptable if dependencies already exist.</p></li></ul><h3>External Deal ID</h3><ul><li><p>Permanent integration identity for one Deal record.</p></li><li><p>May regenerate only while never activated and approved makeup fields change.</p></li><li><p>Once First Activated Date is populated, it never changes.</p></li><li><p>Keep existing automatic collision suffixing: base, <code>-002</code>, <code>-003</code>, etc.</p></li><li><p>Do not add a user-entered Deal Version field.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>Another non-Archived Deal with the same raw makeup remains blocked.</p></li><li><p>Bulk/API writes obey the same uniqueness rule.</p></li><li><p>Multiple Archived historical Deals may share the same historical business makeup because their released technical keys are unique.</p></li><li><p>Closed keeps the makeup reserved.</p></li><li><p>No parent/version Deal hierarchy is added for V1.</p></li></ul><h2>Acceptance criteria</h2><ol><li><p>Active → Paused/Inactive/Closed keeps the raw Makeup Key reserved.</p></li><li><p>Eligible Deal → Archived releases the raw key.</p></li><li><p>Archived keeps its original External Deal ID.</p></li><li><p>Replacement Deal can take the raw Makeup Key and gets the next collision External Deal ID.</p></li><li><p>API/Data Loader cannot bypass the Makeup Key uniqueness rule.</p></li></ol>",
